@meta
id: 21-07
title: The macro that finds its own work
chapter: 21
type: lesson
skills: macro-record, macro-count
par: 56
minutes: 8
vscode: find next, edit, find next, edit, six times, two edits each
open: order.spec.ts

@brief
`OrderService` went async and the spec did not. Six tests still call it
synchronously. Each one needs two edits, on two different lines:

    it('cancels a pending order', () => {            →   it('cancels a pending order', async () => {
      const result = service.cancel('ord_101');      →     const result = await service.cancel('ord_101');

The tests are not on consecutive lines, so `j` is no use as the step
between replays. Put a search inside the macro instead, and choose the
pattern so that it no longer matches once the edit has been made.
Then throw a big count at it.

Two tests in the file are already async and must stay as they are.

@keys
| `/pattern` `Enter` | inside a macro, a search is just another motion |
| `f(` `;` | to the first bracket, then the next one |
| `j0` `f=` `w` | down and to column one, onto the `=`, then the word after it |
| `99@a` | until the search fails |

@hints
Record starting with the search: `/it(.*, () =>` and Enter. It lands on
the `it`. After the edit, that line reads `async () =>`, so the pattern
cannot match it again.
--
From the `it`: `f(;` reaches the empty brackets, `iasync ` and `Esc`.
Then `j0f=w` and `iawait ` and `Esc`. The `0` matters: `j` keeps the
column and `f=` only looks forward. No `j` at the end; the search at
the start is the step.
--
`qa/it(.*, () =><Enter>f(;iasync <Esc>j0f=wiawait <Esc>q` then `99@a`.
The seventh replay searches, finds nothing, and the count dies.

@solution
    qa /it(.*, () => <Enter> f(; iasync  <Esc> j0 f=w iawait  <Esc> q   99@a   :wq<Enter>

Forty-nine keystrokes for twelve edits scattered across a file.

The search is doing two jobs. It is the motion that gets the macro to
the next target, wherever that is, and it is the guard from the last
lesson: when there is nothing left to find, it fails, and the count
stops. Lines you never meant to touch are never visited.

The pattern is chosen with care. `it(.*, () =>` matches a test that
has not yet been made async, and only that. `describe(` blocks do not
contain `it(`; the two tests that are already `async () =>` do not
contain `, () =>`. The edit itself removes the match. That last
property is the important one. A search wraps round to the top of the
file when it runs out of matches below the cursor, so a macro whose
pattern still matches after the edit would cheerfully go round again
and edit the first test a second time. Make the edit consume the
match, and `99@a` is safe. If you cannot, count exactly.

One more thing went into this recording: the `0` after `j`. The first
insert leaves the cursor forty columns in, `j` keeps that column, and
`f=` only looks forward. Without the `0` the macro works on no line at
all. When a recording makes a find on a different line from the one it
started on, reset the column first.

@start order.spec.ts
import { OrderService } from './order.service';

describe('OrderService', () => {
  let service: OrderService;

  beforeEach(() => {
    service = new OrderService(repository, payments);
  });

  it('cancels a pending order', () => {
    const result = service.cancel('ord_101');
    expect(result.status).toBe('CANCELLED');
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', () => {
    const attempt = service.cancel('ord_102');
    expect(attempt).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
  });

  it('marks a packed order as shipped', async () => {
    const result = await service.markShipped('ord_103');
    expect(result.status).toBe('SHIPPED');
  });

  it('refunds inside the window', () => {
    const refund = service.refund('ord_104');
    expect(refund.amount).toBe(1200);
  });

  it('records the reason outside the window', () => {
    const result = service.cancel('ord_105');
    expect(result.cancellationReason).toBe('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
  });

  it('finds an order by id', async () => {
    const order = await service.findOne('ord_106');
    expect(order.id).toBe('ord_106');
  });

  it('throws for an unknown id', () => {
    const attempt = service.findOne('ord_999');
    expect(attempt).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
  });

  it('lists orders for a customer', () => {
    const orders = service.findByCustomer('cus_7');
    expect(orders).toHaveLength(3);
  });
});

@expected order.spec.ts
import { OrderService } from './order.service';

describe('OrderService', () => {
  let service: OrderService;

  beforeEach(() => {
    service = new OrderService(repository, payments);
  });

  it('cancels a pending order', async () => {
    const result = await service.cancel('ord_101');
    expect(result.status).toBe('CANCELLED');
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const attempt = await service.cancel('ord_102');
    expect(attempt).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
  });

  it('marks a packed order as shipped', async () => {
    const result = await service.markShipped('ord_103');
    expect(result.status).toBe('SHIPPED');
  });

  it('refunds inside the window', async () => {
    const refund = await service.refund('ord_104');
    expect(refund.amount).toBe(1200);
  });

  it('records the reason outside the window', async () => {
    const result = await service.cancel('ord_105');
    expect(result.cancellationReason).toBe('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
  });

  it('finds an order by id', async () => {
    const order = await service.findOne('ord_106');
    expect(order.id).toBe('ord_106');
  });

  it('throws for an unknown id', async () => {
    const attempt = await service.findOne('ord_999');
    expect(attempt).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
  });

  it('lists orders for a customer', async () => {
    const orders = await service.findByCustomer('cus_7');
    expect(orders).toHaveLength(3);
  });
});
